<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Labour talks aim to avert national transport strike.</title>
<headline>Labour talks aim to avert national transport strike.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Talks between Bus Eireann and the National Bus and Rail Union begin at Ireland's Labour Relations Commission on Monday in a bid to avert a threatened national transport strike on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The dispute has arisen over Bus Eireann's plans to bring 20 new minibuses into service on Tuesday on suburban routes in Cork, Limerick, Galway and Waterford without union agreement.</p>
<p>Industry sources say the dispute could spread rapidly across national transport group, CIE, affecting other units such as Dublin Bus and rail group Iarnrod Eireann, if it is not resolved.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
